---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Minted & Gone">
  <div class="shell guide-page">
    <section class="field-hero simple-hero"><div class="hero-botanical" aria-hidden="true">☘</div><div class="hero-copy plate-copy"><p class="eyebrow">About this archive</p><h1>What Minted &amp; Gone is</h1><div class="flourish" aria-hidden="true">✦</div><p class="lede">A static-first field guide for NFT marketplaces and their historical states.</p><p>It preserves what disappeared, what remains, and where users or assets went without turning the topic into a price dashboard.</p></div></section>
    <p class="mock-note">The current implementation uses mock layout records only. Treat the archive as a design and validation prototype until records are sourced and reviewed.</p>
    <section class="guide-grid">
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card"><span class="num">01</span><h2>Why it exists</h2><p>NFT marketplaces change quickly. A warm registry can preserve closures, transitions, acquisitions, and surviving artifacts in a way that is useful to researchers and correction-friendly for maintainers.</p></article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card"><span class="num">02</span><h2>What it records</h2><p>Records include identity, scope, chain coverage, frontend status, contract status, asset state, timeline events, source notes, confidence, and review status.</p></article>
      <article class="framed-panel guide-card"><span class="num">03</span><h2>What it does not do</h2><p>Minted &amp; Gone does not provide NFT price data, wallet connection, legal analysis, investment rankings, login, or real-time uptime monitoring.</p></article>
    </section>
    <section class="framed-panel definition-card"><p class="eyebrow">Definition card</p><h2>Field-guide, not dashboard</h2><p>The archive intentionally uses static pages, JSON records, and visible uncertainty. That makes it easier to review claims and harder to mistake mock records for live market signals.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/methodology/">Read methodology</a><a class="btn" href="/submit/">Submit/correct</a></div></section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
